    native_text_struct_field_reads_garbage_int_content_hash_2026-09-07, 0, "2026-11-27 p3sweep2-20261127: doc's exact repro (FileFingerprint.from_file with if val fp = object_fp unwrap + named-field ctor, full src/compiler+src/lib closure) verified byte-identical to the sha256 oracle on: seed interpreter, seed JIT (simple run), Rust pipeline AOT cranelift (the doc's exact lane, run twice with independent builds), pure-Simple AOT llvm, pure-Simple AOT cranelift, and in-process MIR shape checks. The 2026-09-07 garbage non-deterministic int symptom is gone in every lane available on this host. Root cause not bisected (old seeds out of budget) but the evidence is strong: the HEAD seed contains a2884bbb65b fix(seed): bind Some(v) over an erased optional on the JIT - exactly the if val optional-payload-binding shape at the heart of the repro - plus the Sept-Nov optional-payload/field-typing wave. Added test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/native_text_struct_field_content_hash_mir_spec.spl pinning the in-process properties that keep the symptom fixed (content_hash lowers to GetField idx 1 with dest local keeping Opaque(str), size idx 3, 4-field Aggregate ctor, 0 lowering errors) - 4/4 green both modes. Residuals: full-closure pure-Simple AOT probe was killed on this contended host (~7 HIR modules in 20 min; recipe saved in the lane evidence); original report was Linux/aarch64, all evidence here Windows/x86_64 (same lane and flags, OS-specific risk low); two unrelated seed nits recorded (extension-less output verifier false error; MIR-shard worker-reap quirk - use SIMPLE_MIR_SHARDING=0 for small probes). close_evidence reproducer=test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/native_text_struct_field_content_hash_mir_spec.spl prevention=test/01_unit/compiler/backend/text_extern_abi_ptr_len_registry_spec.spl"

